# L §4.4 Only a comparison decides an interval (tally 2.1.7 R3, issue #142; T's SR-9): age(w, d2) is 0 or 1 as w
# falls, and a range's step needs one value: HOLE-IMPRECISE, naming w (g). Its twin with a day for w steps by 1 month
# (g_twin). 2.1.7's first refcore stepped by the interval and crashed (REFCORE-NOT-YET, AttributeError).
=== sr9.tally
model sr9
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "invented"

input w: date

input d1: date

input d2: date

ask g: count(d in d1 .. d2 step age(w, d2) * 1 month)

ask g_twin: count(d in d1 .. d2 step age(d1, d2) * 1 month)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-20) "a day in March"
  d1 = 2026-01-01 "c"
  d2 = 2027-03-10 "c"
=== expect
g: ?"date within window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for a range step" (w)
  cut 2026-12-31
g_twin: 15
  cut 2026-12-31
